hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1500","Ahmad bin Abdah told us, Abbad bin Abbad Al-Muhallabi told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abi Uthman, on the authority of Ubayy bin Ka’b, and he told us Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani, on the authority of al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Musa, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, and this is the hadith of Abbad. He said: There was a man from the Ansar whose house was farthest away. A house in the city, and he was always praying with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so I felt sorry for him and said: O so-and-so, if only you had bought a donkey. It protects you from the rain, raises you from the place, and protects you from the vermin of the earth. He said: By God, I do not like my house to be surrounded by the house of Muhammad, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And peace be upon him. He said: So I carried a burden with him until I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned that to him. He said: So he called him and asked him, so he told him a parable. That, and he mentioned that he had hope in his matter, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Indeed, you will have what you seek,” and in the hadith of Al-San’ani: So I informed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he asked him about that, and he said: O Prophet of God, so that my legacy may be recorded and that I may return to my family. And my approach to him, or as he said: He said: “God has given you all of that, and He has given you all of what you sought,” or as he said"
"1501","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb and Musa bin Abdul-Rahman Al-Masruqi told us, they said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Burayd, on the authority of Abu Burdah, On the authority of Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the people with the greatest reward for prayer are the ones who walk the furthest to it, so they are farthest away.” “The one who waits for the prayer until he prays it with the imam in congregation will have a greater reward than the one who prays it and then sleeps.” They are all one word."
